    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d19-a1-a14">

                <pb facs="0078" n="36" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg36"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#float-left">No. 14.</seg></opener>
                <head>[Official notice from the Gibraltar Chronicle of December 11, 1862.]</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">NOTICE.</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary’s Office, </hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Gibraltar,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1862-12-11"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 11, 1862.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>With reference to the notice in yesterday’s <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Chronicle</hi>, his excellency the <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >governor</hi> has received the following statement from the officer
                    commanding the <hi rendition="#italic">Sumter.</hi></p>
                <pb facs="0079" n="37" xml:id="pg37"/>
                <p>“The Sumter was <hi rendition="#small-caps">bought</hi> and <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">paid</hi> for at New Orleans by the confederate
                    government; that the owners of the then steamer <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Habana</hi> (the <hi rendition="#italic">Sumter)</hi> agreed to the price
                    and terms of sale; and that she was purchased before any vessels had been seized
                    in New Orleans by the confederate government.”</p>
                <p>By command:</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>S. FREELING, <hi rendition="#italic">Colonial
                    Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
